Changes made: the dice numbers were removed and the word list was filtered, so the
vendored copy is a modified subset (6,627 words, sorted alphabetically). Removed
were the four hyphenated entries (the hyphen is our password separator), a short
hand-reviewed blocklist of words that read as profane, sexual, violent or
ridiculous in a credential, and one word of every pair differing by a single
substituted letter, for spoken clarity.

